<title>UK: BSkyB down on worries over convertible issue.</title>
<headline>BSkyB down on worries over convertible issue.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Sky Broadcasting Plc extended recent losses on Monday amid continuing nervousness over News Corporation's planned issue of convertible preferred shares in the satellite broadcaster, traders said.</p>
<p>BSkyB shares closed down 24p at 545 -- its lowest since August 20 -- in active trade of 6.1 million shares.</p>
<p>One trader said there was speculation that details of the issue would be announced later today. &quot;The stock is down on nerves over the convertible pricing,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>No-one at BSkyB was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
